.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CIPHER_GET_NAME 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_name ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_standard_name ,
.Nm OPENSSL_cipher_name ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_bits ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_version ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_description ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_cipher_nid ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_digest_nid ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_handshake_digest ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_kx_nid ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_auth_nid ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_is_aead ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_find ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_id ,
.Nm SSL_CIPHER_get_protocol_id
.Nd get SSL_CIPHER properties
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_name
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_standard_name
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo OPENSSL_cipher_name
.Fa "const char *stdname"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_bits
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fa "int *alg_bits"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_version
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_description
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *cipher"
.Fa "char *buf"
.Fa "int size"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_cipher_nid
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_digest_nid
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft const EVP_MD *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_handshake_digest
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_kx_nid
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_auth_nid
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_is_aead
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft const SSL_CIPHER *
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_find
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "const unsigned char *ptr"
.Fc
.Ft uint32_t
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_id
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Ft uint16_t
.Fo SSL_CIPHER_get_protocol_id
.Fa "const SSL_CIPHER *c"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_name
returns a pointer to the name of
.Fa cipher .
If the
.Fa cipher
is NULL, it returns "(NONE)".
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_standard_name
returns a pointer to the standard RFC name of
.Fa cipher .
If the
.Fa cipher
is NULL, it returns "(NONE)". If the
.Fa cipher
has no standard name, it returns
.Dv NULL .
If
.Fa cipher
was defined in both SSLv3 and TLS, it returns the TLS name.
.Pp
.Fn OPENSSL_cipher_name
returns a pointer to the OpenSSL name of
.Fa stdname .
If the
.Fa stdname
is NULL, or
.Fa stdname
has no corresponding OpenSSL name, it returns "(NONE)". Where both
exist,
.Fa stdname
should be the TLS name rather than the SSLv3 name.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_bits
returns the number of secret bits used for
.Fa cipher .
If
.Fa cipher
is NULL, 0 is returned.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_version
returns string which indicates the SSL/TLS protocol version that first
defined the cipher.
It returns "(NONE)" if
.Fa cipher
is NULL.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_cipher_nid
returns the cipher NID corresponding to
.Fa c .
If there is no cipher (e.g.
for cipher suites with no encryption) then
.Sy NID_undef
is returned.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_digest_nid
returns the digest NID corresponding to the MAC used by
.Fa c
during record encryption/decryption.
If there is no digest (e.g.
for AEAD cipher suites) then
.Sy NID_undef
is returned.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_handshake_digest
returns an EVP_MD for the digest used during the SSL/TLS handshake when
using the SSL_CIPHER
.Fa c .
Note that this may be different to the digest used to calculate the MAC
for encrypted records.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_kx_nid
returns the key exchange NID corresponding to the method used by
.Fa c .
If there is no key exchange, then
.Sy NID_undef
is returned.
If any appropriate key exchange algorithm can be used (as in the case of
TLS 1.3 cipher suites)
.Sy NID_kx_any
is returned.
Examples (not comprehensive):
.Bd -literal
 NID_kx_rsa
 NID_kx_ecdhe
 NID_kx_dhe
 NID_kx_psk
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_auth_nid
returns the authentication NID corresponding to the method used by
.Fa c .
If there is no authentication, then
.Sy NID_undef
is returned.
If any appropriate authentication algorithm can be used (as in the case
of TLS 1.3 cipher suites)
.Sy NID_auth_any
is returned.
Examples (not comprehensive):
.Bd -literal
 NID_auth_rsa
 NID_auth_ecdsa
 NID_auth_psk
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_is_aead
returns 1 if the cipher
.Fa c
is AEAD (e.g.
GCM or ChaCha20/Poly1305), and 0 if it is not AEAD.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_find
returns a
.Sy SSL_CIPHER
structure which has the cipher ID stored in
.Fa ptr .
The
.Fa ptr
parameter is a two element array of
.Vt char ,
which stores the two-byte TLS cipher ID (as allocated by IANA) in
network byte order.
This parameter is usually retrieved from a TLS packet by using functions
like
.Xr SSL_client_hello_get0_ciphers 3 .
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_find
returns NULL if an error occurs or the indicated cipher is not found.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_id
returns the OpenSSL-specific ID of the given cipher
.Fa c .
That ID is not the same as the IANA-specific ID.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_protocol_id
returns the two-byte ID used in the TLS protocol of the given cipher
.Fa c .
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_description
returns a textual description of the cipher used into the buffer
.Fa buf
of length
.Sy len
provided.
If
.Fa buf
is provided, it must be at least 128 bytes.
If
.Fa buf
is NULL it will be allocated using
.Xr OPENSSL_malloc 3 .
If the provided buffer is too small, or the allocation fails,
.Dv NULL
is returned.
.Pp
The string returned by
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_description
consists of several fields separated by whitespace:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It <ciphername>
Textual representation of the cipher name.
.It <protocol version>
The minimum protocol version that the ciphersuite supports, such as
.Sy TLSv1.2 .
Note that this is not always the same as the protocol version in which
the ciphersuite was first defined because some ciphersuites are
backwards compatible with earlier protocol versions.
.It Kx=<key exchange>
Key exchange method such as
.Sy RSA ,
.Sy ECDHE ,
etc.
.It Au=<authentication>
Authentication method such as
.Sy RSA ,
.Sy None ,
etc..
None is the representation of anonymous ciphers.
.It Enc=<symmetric encryption method>
Encryption method, with number of secret bits, such as
.Sy AESGCM(128) .
.It Mac=<message authentication code>
Message digest, such as
.Sy SHA256 .
.El
.Pp
Some examples for the output of
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_description :
.Bd -literal
 ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA256 TLSv1.2 Kx=ECDH     Au=RSA  Enc=AESGCM(256) Mac=AEAD
 RSA-PSK-AES256-CBC-SHA384 TLSv1.0 Kx=RSAPSK   Au=RSA  Enc=AES(256)  Mac=SHA384
.Ed
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_name ,
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_standard_name ,
.Fn OPENSSL_cipher_name ,
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_version
and
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_description
return the corresponding value in a NUL-terminated string for a specific
cipher or "(NONE)" if the cipher is not found.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_bits
returns a positive integer representing the number of secret bits or 0
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_cipher_nid ,
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_digest_nid ,
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_kx_nid
and
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_auth_nid
return the NID value or
.Sy NID_undef
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_handshake_digest
returns a valid
.Sy EVP_MD
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_is_aead
returns 1 if the cipher is AEAD or 0 otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_find
returns a valid
.Sy SSL_CIPHER
structure or NULL if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_id
returns a 4-byte integer representing the OpenSSL-specific ID.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_protocol_id
returns a 2-byte integer representing the TLS protocol-specific ID.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7 ,
.Xr SSL_get_current_cipher 3 ,
.Xr SSL_get_ciphers 3 ,
.Xr openssl-ciphers 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_version
function was updated to always return the correct protocol string in
OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_description
function was changed to return
.Dv NULL
on error, rather than a fixed string, in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_get_handshake_digest
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
.Pp
The
.Fn SSL_CIPHER_standard_name
function was globally available in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
.br
Before OpenSSL 1.1.1, tracing
.Pf ( Sy enable-ssl-trace
argument to Configure) was required to enable this function.
.Pp
The
.Fn OPENSSL_cipher_name
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.1.
